# CH10 — The Smaller Accord. Three communities, three guarantees; SC07 at the trial relay outside Nacre.

@scene CH10_CINDER_FIX once
say narr | The old cooling channel under the garden. Ivo talks two crew members through fitting the bypass, hands in his pockets.
say ivo | Left valve first. No - your other left. Good. Now you know it and I don't have to.
sfx FX010
set accord_cinder
say pell | Heat without the regulator. Slower to warm up. Doesn't hum.
say narr | (Cinderwake's guarantee: heat, maintained by its own crew.)
call CH10_CHECK
@end

@scene CH10_AERIE_FIX once
say narr | The cable brake by the operator's post. Ivo adds a counterweight governor while Corren and the crew hold the basket steady.
sfx FX010
set accord_aerie
say corren | The basket's hanging on its own weight now. No relay.
say edda | Good. Write down how you did it. Put it on a wall, since we love walls.
say narr | (High Aerie's guarantee: stable transit that doesn't depend on a relay.)
call CH10_CHECK
@end

@scene CH10_NACRE once
say sen | Nacre needs the hardest thing: a way to separate consent from pressure. Every dragonborn here has been told what to want by someone with a seal.
say sable | Hearings with no officer in the room. The person speaks, the record keeps it, nobody signs over them.
say oriel | And the answer can change later. That is what the old separation rite understood.
say sen | Then we hold the first hearing tonight. One volunteer. One relay. No hurry.
set accord_nacre
say narr | (Nacre's guarantee: consent heard without institutional pressure.)
call CH10_CHECK
@end

@scene CH10_CHECK
if flag:accord_cinder,flag:accord_aerie,flag:accord_nacre ready
say narr | (Accord visits remaining: Cinderwake's garden bypass, High Aerie's cable brake, Nacre's hearing with Sen.)
end
label ready
objective oriel | All three communities agreed. Meet the volunteer at the trial relay by Nacre's listening pool.
@end

@scene CH10_VOLUNTEER
if flag:accord_cinder,flag:accord_aerie,flag:accord_nacre ready
say volunteer | I'm the first volunteer. When the three towns agree, we'll try the relay. Not before.
end
label ready
say volunteer | Everyone's here. Step up to the relay when you're ready.
@end

@scene CH10_SC07 once
say narr | A trial relay outside Nacre, humming in a stone housing. Ivo has built a distributed circuit around it; Oriel sits with the volunteer.
say ivo | One relay. Kept alive, no captive holding it. The load goes out to the wheel, the cable, the pool - little bits, everywhere.
say oriel | You may stop at any point. Say so, and we stop.
say volunteer | I know.
sfx FX024
wait 0.5
say narr | Slowly - over a long hour - the hum changes key. It doesn't stop. It stops sounding like someone holding their breath.
show rook 26 12 left rook
say rook | One relay. While a hundred keep screaming.
say ivo | This one no longer needs a captive to hold it.
say rook | How many years will you ask them to wait?
say volunteer | Ask me.
say rook | You should not have to accept this.
say volunteer | I have not accepted it. I am choosing how to leave.
say tessa | ...I almost agreed with you, Rook. Almost.
say tessa | The difference is not nothing.
say rook | It will be, to the ones who do not live long enough.
say narr | Rook leaves before anyone can answer. Nera watches him go south.
say nera | He's heading for the old aqueduct under Veyr. The Conduit.
say sable | Voss has been massing soldiers at the Crown Dais for weeks. If Rook forces a synchronisation there -
say dain | Every node at once. Every dragonborn. Nobody asked.
say ivo | One more thing. My plan of the Conduit shows three relay stations. The dais draws load for four. I can't find the fourth.
say oriel | Then we watch for it.
key K_ACCORD_NOTES
set local_release_proven
chapter CH10
objective dain | Stop a forced mass awakening. Enter the Sable Conduit (old aqueduct north of Veyr).
discover L_D09
level_floor 22
hide rook
@end
